    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0498" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg414"/>

                <head>No. 220.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 18,
                        1886</date>. (Received September 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am
                    requested by the Earl of Iddesleigh to state to you that immediate inquiry will
                    be made regarding the action of the officer of the Canadian schooner E. F.
                    Conrad, in the case of the United States schooner Golden Hind, which formed the
                    subject of your note of the 17th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
